    'guide.views.d': '3D relief shows the terrain with rays to the Sun and Earth; Surface puts you on the ground as a helmeted astronaut: walk with W A S D or the on-screen arrows; Globe shows the whole Moon. Beside them, the observer height (2 to 20 m) and the colours: Sun yellow, Earth pink.',
    'guide.answer.t': 'The answer',
    'guide.answer.d': 'One verdict per body: in view or behind the terrain. The sum shows why: the height in the sky minus the terrain in that direction gives the margin. For the Sun, the light reaching a panel. The {chevron} arrow folds the box.',
